  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nStrong high pressure will continue to build into the region \nfrom the northeast, allowing for dry and seasonable conditions \nto continue through early next week. Some residual moisture and \nthe long nights will allow for some morning fog this morning and\nFriday morning, especially in Northwest and North Central Ohio.\nWith the strongest advance of high pressure on Saturday \nmorning, temperatures will drop into the 30s for much of the \narea and some sheltered locations may see upper 20s. Widespread \nto areas of frost will be expected and there will also be some \nfreeze potential. Saturday morning may be the next frost/freeze \nheadline window.",
